OL,3,GNEWSANext wins key appeal to overturn
OL,4,A#30m equal pay ruling
OL,5,
OL,6,FNext has won an appeal allowing it to
OL,7,Fkeep paying warehouse workers a higher
OL,8,Fhourly rate than shop floor staff in a
OL,9,Flong running battle over equal pay.
OL,11,FThe Employment Appeal Tribunal has
OL,12,Foverturned a key part of a landmark
OL,13,Fruling in 2024 which found the retailer
OL,14,Fwas wrong to pay its warehouse staff
OL,15,Fhigher basic pay than shop floor
OL,16,Fworkers for jobs of equal value.
OL,18,FMore than 3,500 current and former
OL,19,Femployees, mainly women, had been set
OL,20,Fto share potentially more than #30m in
OL,21,Fback pay as a result of that judgement.
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
